description.narrative:
APL+ was officially established in 2012 under permit number 399/MoHA from the Ministry of Home Affairs. The association aims to provide a space for people living with HIV and disadvantaged groups to promote their rights and quality of life.
Throughout over 10 years of operation, APL+ has coordinated with government agencies, external organizations, and civil society to drive work on rights, access to health services, various welfare programs, and livelihood promotion. Key experiences of the association include:
• Managingprojects related to health, rights to access services, and promoting good livelihoods in communities across 12 provinces;
• Implementing projects on life skills development and adaptation to climate change;
• Providing vocational training to youth and disadvantaged communities;
• Producing communication materials, promoting community participation, and driving public policy advocacy.
• Agricultural Experience: The association has implemented practical work in areas such as Xieng Ngeun and Xaychamphone districts regarding adaptation to climate change and building knowledge about the environment.
Main Activities of the Association
- Promote health and quality of life for people living with HIV and disadvantaged communities;
- Organize prevention activities and provide education on HIV/AIDS and general health;
- Provide mental health counseling services and home visits for people living with HIV;
- Produce communication materials and promote community participation in policy advocacy and various services;
- Build knowledge and promote adaptation to climate change and environmental conservation;
- Provide vocational training and promote employment opportunities for youth and communities.
Project Goal:
To create guidelines forbuilding knowledge and raising awareness about cultivating crops free from toxic chemicals.
To build knowledge and understanding regarding the use of chemicals in vegetable cultivation in order to reduce healthimpacts.
To promote safe vegetable cultivation and the long-term reduction of chemical residues.
Objectives:
To raise awareness about cultivating crops free from toxic chemicals.
To promote knowledge on the correct and health-safe use of chemicals.
To raise awareness about cultivating home garden vegetables safely, free from chemicals, and improving production quality.
